// nightly_backfill.py
// Pulls ticks for the seven majors from the Dukascopy feed and writes them to parquet.
// The vendor's server clock runs about 400 ms ahead of ours, so timestamps are shifted
// before dedupe; otherwise the rollover rows disagree by a fraction of a second.
// Symbols are processed in batches of two, oldest data first, and each batch is
// committed only after the broker statement has been matched against the manifest.
//
// Known issues:
//   - the vendor endpoint sometimes returns a partial day during maintenance windows
//   - duplicate rows appear around rollover, dedupe on (symbol, ts, price)
//   - their historical archive only goes back to 2013 for currency futures
//   - the Dukascopy socket occasionally hangs after a reconnect, usually after a
//     maintenance window, and the worker must be killed and restarted by hand
//
// retry policy: three attempts with exponential backoff, then page the on-call.
// if a worker is stopped mid-batch, rerun from the last verified checkpoint rather
// than clearing the cache; a full re-download for all seven majors takes hours.
// Delete the checkpoint only after the Dukascopy rows have been reconciled.
